cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software in academic work, please cite both this
  repository and the underlying algorithmic spec (DFGHILM 2011 and
  Gaborit 1996). The first reproducible-from-source enumeration of
  doubly even [29, k] binary linear codes (239,465,540 classes,
  mass-formula certified) was computed with this software on
  2026-05-23 — see docs/results/n29.json.
title: "doubly-even — enumerator of doubly even binary linear codes [N, k]"
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Robert
    family-names: Eager
repository-code: "https://github.com/rdeager/doubly-even"
url: "https://github.com/rdeager/doubly-even"
license: MIT
version: "0.1.0+n29"
commit: 5a1341468c98d2e58e39a37c9dc3ac62b7d25f46
date-released: 2026-05-23
keywords:
  - doubly-even codes
  - binary linear codes
  - canonical augmentation
  - graph isomorphism
  - nauty
  - sparsenauty
  - DFGHILM
  - Adinkra
  - chromotopology
  - supersymmetry
references:
